From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qpsx: expose low-rate runtime progress for smoke tests

The SF2000 QPSX smoke test must distinguish sustained emulation from a core
that produces only the first few VBlanks and then stops.  Emit one marker per
60 retro_run calls, but only when the existing debug_log configuration flag is
enabled.  Normal physical-device configurations keep debug logging disabled,
so this adds no normal log or timing overhead.

--- a/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
+++ b/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
@@ -3650,2 +3650,5 @@
     run_frame_count++;
     input_debug_counter++;
+    if (g_debug_log_enabled && (run_frame_count % 60 == 0)) {
+        XLOG("retro_run progress: frame %d", run_frame_count);
+    }
